{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars","id":78496,"title":"A Couple Simple Thoughts on Lunars","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-24T12:17:58-08:00","id":78496,"title":"A Couple Simple Thoughts on Lunars","content":"I mentioned this in the other current Lunars thread, but no one commented on it, so I'm posting it in its old thread.<br /> <br /> I preferred the first edition Lunars concept that focused on the Survival of the Fittest mentality of Lunars over the Stewards of Creation concept that 2nd edition promoted. I always get bugged by the quasi-New Age mentality where nature is nice, because nature is far more often brutal and vicious. This is just a pet peeve of mine, so perhaps I'm in the minority. And I fully understand that second edition Lunars were still very savage.<br /> <br /> I also preferred the stat-building mechanics that came with multiple purchases of Deadly Beastman over the shopping for Wyld mutations idea from 2nd Edition. I applauded the improved variety Second Edition allowed, but I like Lunars with huge stats. I fully comprehend that a bonus dot of Dexterity is probably worth two dots in Strength or Stamina. I merely have a lot of affection for great big, tough-to-damage characters and find them more fun than the guys with supreme technique and precision. If you a little about Ultimate Fighting Championship, I'd rather watch a UFC rerun with Chuck Liddell than one with BJ Henderson. Liddell is a household name, but Henderson was a crazy fast and hard to hit champion from the light divisions.<br /> <br /> I know this is just about my personal preferences, so this thread will die pretty fast, and its death will make way for smarter conversations. I'm just curious about what others think about these things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have irregular access to the Web, so if you want to contact me, PM my account or email me at <a href=\"/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#d4b1a6bdbfbcb5a0bdbab1ba94adb5bcbbbbfab7bbb9\"><span class=\"__cf_email__\" data-cfemail=\"6e0b1c0705060f1a07000b002e170f060101400d0103\">[email&#160;protected]</span></a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/876-tsallak","name":"Tsallak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T12:44:25-08:00","id":78511,"title":"","content":"As an ideology, it's probably not very sensible to be social Darwinists when your opponents are not just social Darwinists, but also have most of the world locked down and under their control. You'll probably want something a bit more flexible while you're waiting to spring the latest trap in your campaign of asymmetric warfare against the Realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T15:15:35-08:00","id":78676,"title":"","content":"The problem with both the survival-of-the-fittest Lunars and the stewards-of-creation Lunars was that it presented them as caricatures. Both obsessions came off as basically pretty ridiculous and disconnected from any of the realities of the setting -- it felt like they had an ideology crudely stamped into their brain by an author to make them like WoD Garou or to fit a specific role.<br /> <br /> Lunars shouldn't be defined by NATURE IS VICIOUS or NATURE IS NICE; they should have coherent political and social reasons for believing what they do and behaving the way they do.<br /> <br /> As far as big stats go... I mean, yeah, obviously, that's always going to be a part of Lunars to an extent, but Exalted's dice mechanics tend to break apart when you have people persistently throwing around too many dice, so it has to be approached very carefully.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T15:39:06-08:00","id":78713,"title":"","content":"Well said. I often read topics of 'What Distinguishes a Solar Exaltation from a Lunar Exaltation' and think... time, that's pretty much it. Amazing people who deserve an Exaltation are going to merit a second glance from a reincarnating Celestial Soul regardless of whether they are country bumpkins or erudite scholars. I seriously doubt the Lunar Exaltation has a litmus test for screening out people that don't appreciate a particular ideology regarding nature and humanities place within it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T10:50:05-08:00","id":81132,"title":"","content":"Maddy, I don't know who you think said something well. I suspect it's Aquillion, and he does write very well, both here and on just about every other topic I've seen him post on (my apologies if you're female, Aquillion). You're no slouch, either. And Saur's point is highly intelligent. I feel a little silly that I didn't think of that myself. You reminded me of what the Lunars agreed upon from their book's first chapter. That's what their big scheme (The Silver Project? I don't remember its title) is for, after all. I only recalled that they disliked both the current Realm and the High First Age because they think humans should be independent<br /> <br /> For the record, I don't think all Lunars have to be berserk twelve-foot savages; your Lunar could be as short as six foot four. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I just think that given how intense the natural world is and Luna's own tendencies (one of his/her aspects is an insane murderess with sickles and horns!), I'd favor barbarism over gentleness. The idea that all Lunars must have something to protect as their motivation struck me as less than intuitive, and probably an artifact from the gameline that inspired them.<br /> <br /> As for dice caps, I have nothing against them. I certainly didn't mean that I wanted Lunars to be the ultimate badguy mashers, either, though I doubt none of you interpreted what I wrote that way. Who cares that they're inspired from Werewolf, who were probably the best badguy mashers of the Old WoD? I just liked that they had that asset among their powers. I doubt First Edition Lunars could outfight first edition Solars, even with the Lunars' higher Attributes. With second edition, I suspect (I'm not sure; I have never played nor ran a game of Exalted) Lunars weren't quite as powerful, but I could easily be wrong. Solars and their corrupted cousins are meant to be more powerful than Lunars. That's fine. I just liked that Lunars had a couple nifty things that Solars and so on can't do. I know that's still true, and it will remain true. I just liked that one of those things was a big stat boost the others couldn't match (well, without Strength-Increasing Exercise).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have irregular access to the Web, so if you want to contact me, PM my account or email me at <a href=\"/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#0c697e6567646d78656269624c756d646363226f6361\"><span class=\"__cf_email__\" data-cfemail=\"3d584f5456555c49545358537d445c555252135e5250\">[email&#160;protected]</span></a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/876-tsallak","name":"Tsallak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T19:49:18-08:00","id":81371,"title":"","content":"A simple thought on Lunars:<br /> <br /> Today I thought to myself, &quot;I am going to make a sneaky rat lunar.'<br /> <br /> For a Solar exalted, this would mean I'd need to put points in dexterity, stealth, and larceny, and buy stealth and larceny charms.<br /> <br /> For a Lunar, it means putting points in dexterity, stealth, and larceny, and then realizing there are no dexterity charms that help with sneaking someplace, breaking into places, or opening locks. The best I could find was an appearance charm that might help me escape detection after people are already alert to my PC's presence and looking for her, and some wits charms that might help me pickpocket things.<br /> <br /> I find it odd there are no charms that help you blend into your environment or muffle the noises as they're both very animalish.<br /> <br /> Anyways, I ended up pulling out my copy of Werewolf: The Forsaken, and making a starting Irraka instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":296,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","user":"hippokrene","date":". 02-27-2014, 10:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T20:37:22-08:00","id":81393,"title":"","content":"I really loved the Forsaken Stealth gifts. Very &quot;werewolf / monster horror&quot;.<br /> <br /> The first one eliminates your scent. Doesn't often come up in horror movies, but it's essential in a werewolf's line of work.<br /> <br /> The second one allows you to run without a sound. You could be barreling at full speed over gravel in your giant wolf form, without a whisper. Thus, you can sneak up behind people or around them by darting from cover to cover. In movies, this is the audience watching the monster approach while the victim is always looking away at the wrong moment.<br /> <br /> Finally, &quot;hide in plain sight&quot;. As long as you don't move, they don't see you. Essentially eliminates the need for cover, while still necessitating the Silent Running trick for moving in while the victim looks away.<br /> <br /> Compared to that comprehensive pack of tricks, the next two are rather forgettable. One turns you into a two-dimensional shadow, and I don't even remember the other one. It might have been better to have some sort of Vanishing From the Mind's Eye retro-active stealth trick, where anyone who sees you later forgets you were there. Or something that let you better employ the third Gift against multiple watchful victims who would otherwise not give you enough opportunities to run silently and unseen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T21:17:17-08:00","id":81403,"title":"","content":"Uratha also had a subset of Evasion for things like that. Make people blurt out things they really shouldn't like Pam from Archer, interfere with sight, play dead, know when people are trying to trick you (cue the poorly-drawn goofy macro), and sing panic into people. When the shit is about to hit the fan, they help you get the hell out of Dodge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T01:36:44-08:00","id":81473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tsallak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars#post78496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always get bugged by the quasi-New Age mentality where nature is nice, because nature is far more often brutal and vicious.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Altruism_in_animals\" target=\"_blank\">Nnnnnnope.</a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T01:53:58-08:00","id":81476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=81473#post81473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Altruism_in_animals\" target=\"_blank\">Nnnnnnope.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Altruism and viciousness aren't mutually exclusive. <br /> <br /> Here in Australia the natural forces team up to exterminate you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T02:05:33-08:00","id":81477,"title":"","content":"The highest amount of biomass is from plants, so the truest statement is 'nature is lazy.'<br /> <br /> When was the last time you saw a phytoplankton hold down a full time job? It just floats there, sucking up sunlight from honest, hardworking Americans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T02:18:54-08:00","id":81479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=81371#post81371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A simple thought on Lunars:<br /> <br /> Today I thought to myself, &quot;I am going to make a sneaky rat lunar.'<br /> <br /> For a Solar exalted, this would mean I'd need to put points in dexterity, stealth, and larceny, and buy stealth and larceny charms.<br /> <br /> For a Lunar, it means putting points in dexterity, stealth, and larceny, and then realizing there are no dexterity charms that help with sneaking someplace, breaking into places, or opening locks. The best I could find was an appearance charm that might help me escape detection after people are already alert to my PC's presence and looking for her, and some wits charms that might help me pickpocket things.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would think that a vital point of playing a sneaky rat Lunar would be <i>learning how to turn into a rat</i>.<br /> <br /> Just a hunch!<br /> <br /> More seriously: Lunars do have sneaky charms, but they tend to not be in Dexterity. And, honestly, I think that's a good thing -- you're not seriously suggesting you want Dexterity to do even <i>more</i>, are you? Given the way abilities are structured and the desire to give them a distinctive theme, it makes sense to me that the writers decided that Lunar stealth focused more on (Manipulation, Charisma, etc) trickery and illusion effects rather than Dexterity-style &quot;I sneak real well&quot; charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 02-28-2014, 05:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T02:51:54-08:00","id":81484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=81479#post81479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would think that a vital point of playing a sneaky rat Lunar would be <i>learning how to turn into a rat</i>.<br /> <br /> Just a hunch!</div> </div> </div> </div>Which would be great, if the advice on how to handle shape-shifting wasn't 'give some bonus successes'. Given the suggested range and that turning into an insect is a thing, you're probably looking at a benefit on one or two successes ... about equivalent to the use of your excellency. Not to be sneezed at necessarily, but hardly worthwhile as the key point in your character concept, and very quickly going to fall behind supernaturally aware characters' ability to spot you. <br /> <br /> I pretty much agree that shape-shifting should be a useful tool, but per the rules at the moment it's about worth a strong equipment bonus. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T02:58:28-08:00","id":81486,"title":"","content":"I'm going to disagree that turning into a rat is just as good as having actual stealth and larceny charms.<br /> <br /> Turning into a rat doesn't let me open locks with a touch, walk through closed doors, make it so no one sees me, or allow me to vanish immediately while removing the memory of my being there from other's mind. It doesn't make sure that I leave no trace of physical evidence of my passing, or let me hear through walls (and no, rat ears don't let you do this), pick a lock even if I have no tools whatsoever. It doesn't let me see perfectly in the dark, suppress all sound of my movement, or automatically distract guards/servants/marks.<br /> <br /> Yes, being a small animal opens up unique and interesting possibilities. No one is denying that. There's also a lot of stuff that <i>shapeshifting doesn't do</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T05:07:32-08:00","id":81523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuddenThunder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=81476#post81476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here in Australia the natural forces team up to exterminate you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder how &quot;survival of the fittest&quot; lines up with the existence of a class of mammals that spends the first few months of its life living in a specialized pouch designed to nurture and protect them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T05:18:50-08:00","id":81525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuddenThunder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=81484#post81484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which would be great, if the advice on how to handle shape-shifting wasn't 'give some bonus successes'.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine that it will certainly help when animals are given more comprehensive features.<br /> <br /> Although I'll admit, comprehensive mechanical representation of a rat being &quot;sneaky&quot; strikes me as a tad excessive. I mean, unless people are actively looking for rats, you need systemic representation of that about as much as you need it for going about the street, or dressing as a servant. Or for a rat to get into a place, as much as you need the system for walking through a door (although a special Dexterity check to slip through a tiny hole would be in order).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=81486#post81486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to disagree that turning into a rat is just as good as having actual stealth and larceny charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, probably, but those are the breaks if Lunars don't get Stealth and Larceny Charms.<br /> <br /> Turning into a rat probably isn't as good as what a Solar could do, but it's better than somebody with no Charms at all, and you generally won't have to pay experience for it.<br /> <br /> Shapeshifting might not be as powerful as Charms, and a Lunar who doesn't use much shapeshifting is probably not necessarily less powerful than one who does, but it does go some ways to helping individual Lunars be versatile. A Lunar whose character concept precludes them placing much emphasis on combat Charms <i>or</i> Abilities can still turn into a tyrant lizard.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Turning into a rat doesn't let me open locks with a touch, walk through closed doors, make it so no one sees me, or allow me to vanish immediately while removing the memory of my being there from other's mind. It doesn't make sure that I leave no trace of physical evidence of my passing, or let me hear through walls (and no, rat ears don't let you do this), pick a lock even if I have no tools whatsoever. It doesn't let me see perfectly in the dark, suppress all sound of my movement, or automatically distract guards/servants/marks.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Should</i> Lunars do all of these? I mean, sure, there are some that feel suited for them, but others are already Solar tricks.<br /> <br /> In particular, are you still talking about Dexterity when you suggest removing the memory of your presence from somebody's mind?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T05:52:43-08:00","id":81538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=81525#post81525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although I'll admit, comprehensive mechanical representation of a rat being &quot;sneaky&quot; strikes me as a tad excessive. I mean, unless people are actively looking for rats, you need systemic representation of that about as much as you need it for going about the street, or dressing as a servant. Or for a rat to get into a place, as much as you need the system for walking through a door (although a special Dexterity check to slip through a tiny hole would be in order).</div> </div> </div> </div>Certainly, but as you say it has to be one way or another. If there's not a satisfying set of Lunar sneaking Charms then shapeshifting has to be worth more than a couple of successes assigned ad-hoc. If you don't want to go into that much detail for animals (to be hijacked into shape-shifting) then we need available avenues via Charms. Either is fine, but you've got to do one. 'Go shapeshift' isn't an answer when shapeshifting is essentially a dice-adder.<br /> <br /> Maybe it's just a case of Lunar Luck. They've got brilliant Charms for hiding other things. Possibly the best available Charms for hiding and army(!). It's just that their options for hiding themselves are limited to The Spider's Trap Door and maybe Clover Can't Be Found. <br /> <br /> One imagines that the new Lunars will open avenues, one way or another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T06:08:31-08:00","id":81545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=81525#post81525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In particular, are you still talking about Dexterity when you suggest removing the memory of your presence from somebody's mind?</div> </div> </div> </div>She was never really talking about Dexterity, but about Lunars lacking Charms for sneaking and being pretty unintuitive besides.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T06:25:08-08:00","id":81554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=81403#post81403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...play dead...</div> </div> </div> </div>On that note, I'm starting to get bugged by how many WoD/Exalted splats have &quot;play dead&quot; as either a written character power (Mage, Changeling, Demon, Werewolf, Slasher, Abyssal), or as an innate feature of the character (Vampire, seriously, just sit still without spending blood points on acting alive), yet never acknowledge genre-savvy players going to drastic measures &quot;to be sure.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> There needs to be a sidebar or something.<br /> <br /> Anyway, back on topic: <i>there are no &quot;simple thoughts&quot; on Lunars.</i> It's one big timey-wimey mess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T06:33:43-08:00","id":81557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=81545#post81545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">She was never really talking about Dexterity, but about Lunars lacking Charms for sneaking and being pretty unintuitive besides.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's bugged me for quite a while how front-loaded Lunars have been. Shapeshifting lets them do almost anything at chargen, then that tremendous front-loaded power is used to justify why Lunars can't get useful and interesting charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T06:35:59-08:00","id":81559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=81525#post81525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, probably, but those are the breaks if Lunars don't get Stealth and Larceny Charms.<br /> <br /> Turning into a rat probably isn't as good as what a Solar could do, but it's better than somebody with no Charms at all, and you generally won't have to pay experience for it.<br /> <br /> Shapeshifting might not be as powerful as Charms, and a Lunar who doesn't use much shapeshifting is probably not necessarily less powerful than one who does, but it does go some ways to helping individual Lunars be versatile. A Lunar whose character concept precludes them placing much emphasis on combat Charms <i>or</i> Abilities can still turn into a tyrant lizard.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alternatively, even though I can turn into a tyrant lizard, the book gives me a ton of combat charms. Yes, I can turn into a rat, but a few charms to help me sneak around unnoticed and break into places would be appreciated.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Should</i> Lunars do all of these? I mean, sure, there are some that feel suited for them, but others are already Solar tricks. </div> </div> </div>Half the charms I listed are Solar and the other half are Dragon-Blooded. No, Lunars don't need all of them, but when a newly created Dragon-Blood is better at sneaking around and stealing stuff than a Lunar, there is something wrong here. When going to Werewolf: The Forsaken nets me a better sneaky rat thief than the Lunar core, there is something wrong here.<br /> <br /> Oh, and finding charms I wanted was <i>so much</i> faster when it came to Solars, Werewolves, and Dragon-Blooded. The Lunar charm layout is like the Infernal charm layout with all the fun sucked out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In particular, are you still talking about Dexterity when you suggest removing the memory of your presence from somebody's mind? </div> </div> </div>Then stick it in perception or appearance, but given that dexterity + stealth is the basic roll, you'd think they'd have some stuff for stealth.<br /> <br /> And here's the thing: Sneaking completely falls within Lunar themes. Sure, they can be the raging horror that falls upon you and tears you limb from limb -- that's awesome.<br /> <br /> I want to be the the shadow that drifts into your house to suck out your child's breath as you dream fitfully in the other room. I want to be something skittering, half glimpsed in the darkness. I want to toy with someone until their friends swear they've gone mad... and then that person disappear without a trace. Or maybe they're still there, but it's really me now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":296,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","user":"hippokrene","date":". 02-28-2014, 09:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T06:41:46-08:00","id":81560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zironic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=81557#post81557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shapeshifting lets them do almost anything at chargen</div> </div> </div> </div>Does it though? Really?<br /> <br /> Given the guidelines provided for shape-changing, what does shape-shanging let them do beyond the scope of their Charms that a dice adder or decent equipment wouldn't?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T06:42:41-08:00","id":81561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=81559#post81559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then stick it in perception or appearance, but given that dexterity + stealth is the basic roll, you'd think they'd have some stuff for stealth.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be pretty neat if 'moving with precision' was moved to perception on the System level so Dexterity could stop doing everything. I've been checking out Blood and Smoke lately and they seem to have managed to avoid &quot;godstats&quot; which in turn would make it easier to make attribute based trees that make sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T06:48:50-08:00","id":81565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zironic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=81561#post81561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It would be pretty neat if 'moving with precision' was moved to perception on the System level so Dexterity could stop doing everything. I've been checking out Blood and Smoke lately and they seem to have managed to avoid &quot;godstats&quot; which in turn would make it easier to make attribute based trees that make sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T06:50:26-08:00","id":81568,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuddenThunder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=81560#post81560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does it though? Really?<br /> <br /> Given the guidelines provided for shape-changing, what does shape-shanging let them do beyond the scope of their Charms that a dice adder or decent equipment wouldn't?</div> </div> </div> </div>They can infiltrate almost any area by turning into a cat/puppy/rat etc, they can fast-travel by turning into birds, they can become combat monsters by turning into a Tyrant Lizard, dive the depths of the ocean by becoming a shark etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T07:10:37-08:00","id":81577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zironic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=81568#post81568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They can infiltrate almost any area by turning into a cat/puppy/rat etc, they can fast-travel by turning into birds, they can become combat monsters by turning into a Tyrant Lizard, dive the depths of the ocean by becoming a shark etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>The guidelines suggest they can do all of these things badly ... by Exalted standards. <br /> <br /> \u200bShapechangng is worth between one and three successes, as per MoEP:L pg 129. That is to say, it's approximately worth a full-force Excellency.<br /> <br /> We've been discussing the deficencies of Lunar sneaky Charms, and they have a suite of combat oprions that's worth more than a dice adder. While it's all very well to say they can do 'X' and 'Y' and 'Z' by shapeshifting there no real case that they're better off doing than than using Charms. Is it really an argument to say that any genre a character might want to explore should be satisfied with +3 successes from shape-changing instead of considered Charms?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T07:37:22-08:00","id":81588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuddenThunder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=81577#post81577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The guidelines suggest they can do all of these things badly ... by Exalted standards.<br /> <br /> \u200bShapechangng is worth between one and three successes, as per MoEP:L pg 129. That is to say, it's approximately worth a full-force Excellency.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're reading that sidebar wrong. The sidebar says that they do these things near perfectly, they're all unrolled effects. The sidebar further explains that beyond unrolled effects they also get a 1-3 success bonus on appropriate rolls which is in addition to the completely silly attributes they get if they have something as a Tyrant Lizard as their totem, as explained on page 128.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T07:46:43-08:00","id":81591,"title":"","content":"If a tyrant lizard Lunar can have a Strength Charm for super strength, Stamina Charm for armor, and Charisma Charm for an even scarier roar, a rat Lunar can have a Dexterity Charm for making no sound and squeezing through cracks, a Wits Charm for avoiding sight, and an Appearance Charm for leaving no scent (or a misleading one).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T07:53:27-08:00","id":81594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=81525#post81525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Should</i> Lunars do all of these? I mean, sure, there are some that feel suited for them, but others are already Solar tricks.<br /> In particular, are you still talking about Dexterity when you suggest removing the memory of your presence from somebody's mind?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they should be able to do most of those, but I think the reasons should be a bit more oblique. I like to think of Lunars as creatures of stories. Not creatures that tell themselves into stories, like the Fair Folk, but creatures that others tell stories about. They are urban legends, myths, and creepy campfire stories (and often more than one of each). Lunars are the monsters you never see; even in broad daylight what you see may be no more than the fin above the surface of the water. So yeah, they should be capable of almost anything (in theory), because even the most obvious Full Moon should have hidden depths that keep his enemies guessing.<br /> <br /> The challenge is not finding the things they can do, but finding the thematic space to build those things so that they aren't just the hated &quot;Silver Solars&quot; with the same charms only worse/more expensive/more limited etc. Just because Solars have a trick does not mean that Lunars can't do the same thing, they are just going to need a different method of getting there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":".  Removed needless comparison to Solars 02-28-2014, 10:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T08:10:49-08:00","id":81598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=81591#post81591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a tyrant lizard Lunar can have a Strength Charm for super strength, Stamina Charm for armor, and Charisma Charm for an even scarier roar, a rat Lunar can have a Dexterity Charm for making no sound and squeezing through cracks, a Wits Charm for avoiding sight, and an Appearance Charm for leaving no scent (or a misleading one).</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I think it would be easier to balance if Lunars didn't get &quot;Turn into almost anything!&quot; at chargen, but instead 'Turn into small things like Rats' was a charm in the stealth tree and 'turn into fast things like Cheetahs' was part of the move fast tree etc. It's the front-loaded part that makes it so awkward and also makes it hard for Lunars to distinguish themselves from eachother.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T08:21:06-08:00","id":81603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zironic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=81588#post81588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're reading that sidebar wrong. The sidebar says that they do these things near perfectly, they're all unrolled effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>The sidebar says:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoEP:Lunrs, pg 129</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">When a Lunar uses these<br /> innate abilities, it should manifest as automatic success<br /> or, when a roll is dramatically appropriate, bonus<br /> successes ranging from +1 to +3.</div> </div> </div> </div>No-one is arguing that lunars should not be able to swoop past Sten the guardsman in the shape of swift, scale the formidable wall of Castello Auriga, or butt their shoulder to the gate of the dread fortress. The question is 'is this a task in which the Lunar's success or failure matters' (the very definition of a roll being dramatically appropriate) and the result is that in any situation that the ST shouldn't be willing to give you an autosuccess anyhow you might just as well use shape-shifting as your Excellency. <br /> <br /> After all, it's not as though there isn't an autosuccess rule in the core book that you can often buy into using a dice-adder.<br /> <br /> Or ... is there ... ?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T09:12:47-08:00","id":81617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuddenThunder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=81603#post81603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No-one is arguing that lunars should not be able to swoop past Sten the guardsman in the shape of swift, scale the formidable wall of Castello Auriga, or butt their shoulder to the gate of the dread fortress. The question is 'is this a task in which the Lunar's success or failure matters' (the very definition of a roll being dramatically appropriate) and the result is that in any situation that the ST shouldn't be willing to give you an autosuccess anyhow you might just as well use shape-shifting as your Excellency.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not the definition of dramatically appropriate. By that measure you would be rolling every single breath you take, because failure would have extreme consequences. Dramatically appropriate is when the dramatical tension is interesting and appropriate. For instance if they are actually searching for a shapeshifter actively, then having the rat form give you 1-2 bonus successes* makes sense, if they're not actively looking then rolling makes no sense, they're not looking for rats or mosquitios or whatever you might have turned into.<br /> <br /> *Which don't count against die-caps btw making them something you get to use in addition to charm die bonuses, not instead of.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, it doesn't matter how many thousand dice you can add through charms, you'll never breathe underwater, weave webs, inject deadly venom with your bite or fly like a swallow which are all abilities that Shapeshifting gives the chargen Lunar that never translate to 1-3 bonus sux, even if the Lunar book itself is a bit confused on the subject (What possible roll would having a poison bite give bonus sux to?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T10:24:06-08:00","id":81649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zironic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=81617#post81617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By that measure you would be rolling every single breath you take, because failure would have extreme consequences.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? I think you know very well that's not what I meant. At the very least we can agree that rolling to breathe is neither dramatic nor appropriate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zironic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=81617#post81617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Which don't count against die-caps btw making them something you get to use in addition to charm die bonuses, not instead of.</div> </div> </div> </div>So something like the Daiklave/Armour/Cloak of Shadows that any other character is able to access without changing form? Ultimately what matters is simply not more dice added on, whether they come from Charms or shape-shifting or equipment. All Exalts in their area of expertise are able to move past that ... except, for some reason, Lunars in odd areas with no clear rationale. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zironic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=81617#post81617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Furthermore, it doesn't matter how many thousand dice you can add through charms, you'll never breathe underwater, weave webs, inject deadly venom with your bite or fly like a swallow</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? Because it seems like the Water anima and Element-Resisting Prana (which are both available to starting characters) allow you to breathe underwater. Joint Wounding Attack and Prey-Hobbling Bite immobilise enemies, if not specifically weave spiderwebs, and the entire Scorpion and Toad branch deals with poisons. All of this is accessible to starting characters so the question remains: where is shepeshifting a comparable or better alternative to taking Charms?<br /> <br /> (I don't think it actually is, and that's a flaw of the 2E Lunar design. But if we want Lunars in 3E to approch shape-shifting as a worthwhile path there has to be something ther worth pursuing and that probably means rules for animals in some sort of detail).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T10:35:35-08:00","id":81657,"title":"","content":"Levi, I couldn't access your link this time because of time constraints, and the fact that when I read these things where I live (I have to the library for web access), I have to save them in text form, which clearly means no links work. I'll get to it.<br /> <br /> This has really taken off! But certainly Lunars should have stealth capabilities. I think more predators rely on stealth and surprise than just barreling in at full speed and beating the snot out whatever's there. I'm pretty sure that's what almost the whole cat family does (not just housecats, but pumas, tigers, cheetahs and so on).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have irregular access to the Web, so if you want to contact me, PM my account or email me at <a href=\"/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#3d584f5456555c49545358537d445c555252135e5250\"><span class=\"__cf_email__\" data-cfemail=\"d8bdaab1b3b0b9acb1b6bdb698a1b9b0b7b7f6bbb7b5\">[email&#160;protected]</span></a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/876-tsallak","name":"Tsallak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T10:52:07-08:00","id":81668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tsallak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=81657#post81657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This has really taken off! But certainly Lunars should have stealth capabilities. I think more predators rely on stealth and surprise than just barreling in at full speed and beating the snot out whatever's there. I'm pretty sure that's what almost the whole cat family does (not just housecats, but pumas, tigers, cheetahs and so on).</div> </div> </div> </div>Most certainly. But does the current Lunar design support that and (probably more important) will the X3 Lunar design support it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T11:05:29-08:00","id":81673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=81594#post81594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like to think of Lunars as creatures of stories. Not creatures that tell themselves into stories, like the Fair Folk, but creatures that others tell stories about.</div> </div> </div> </div>People tell stories about freaking everything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are urban legends, myths, and creepy campfire stories (and often more than one of each).</div> </div> </div> </div>Which stories? What things in particular?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars are the monsters you never see; even in broad daylight what you see may be no more than the fin above the surface of the water.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's pretty vague.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to be the the shadow that drifts into your house to suck out your child's breath as you dream fitfully in the other room. I want to be something skittering, half glimpsed in the darkness. I want to toy with someone until their friends swear they've gone mad... and then that person disappear without a trace. Or maybe they're still there, but it's really me now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't actually object to Lunars having sneaky Charms and general methodologies, but something about the motifs in this particular phrasing just doesn't sit right with me.<br /> <br /> It feels too much like the Fair Folk.<br /> <br /> Surely there's got to be a way to make sneaky, sinister Lunars fit in with the established umbrella motifs without straying too far out or being too vague...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T11:47:13-08:00","id":81702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuddenThunder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=81649#post81649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? Because it seems like the Water anima and Element-Resisting Prana (which are both available to starting characters) allow you to breathe underwater. Joint Wounding Attack and Prey-Hobbling Bite immobilise enemies, if not specifically weave spiderwebs, and the entire Scorpion and Toad branch deals with poisons. All of this is accessible to starting characters so the question remains: where is shepeshifting a comparable or better alternative to taking Charms?</div> </div> </div> </div>Tell me again how the Water Anima, ERP, JWA, PHB and Scorpion and Toad are die adders, I'd like to hear all about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T11:52:35-08:00","id":81707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=81673#post81673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't actually object to Lunars having sneaky Charms and general methodologies, but something about the motifs in this particular phrasing just doesn't sit right with me.<br /> <br /> It feels too much like the Fair Folk.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's a bit Raksha. I think of stealthy Lunars and I think of Alien, or Predator, or the Thing. Knowing that you're hunted by something but not knowing what it is, or where it is. Slowly being consumed one by one, not because it can't take you all at once but because it wants to play with you. Maybe it wants to let one of you get away and run back to the Realm with stories of how it terrorised you. Or maybe you'll be the last one left and you'll worship it, because what else can you possibly do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T12:02:44-08:00","id":81711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuddenThunder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=81649#post81649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All of this is accessible to starting characters so the question remains: where is shepeshifting a comparable or better alternative to taking Charms?</div> </div> </div> </div>Question remains? That's a new question. Before you were arguing shapeshifting was merely a die adder, now you're using half a dozen charms to emulate the various effects availible through shape-shifting.<br /> <br /> However the problem is that Shapeshifting or Charms is never a question, Lunars get the shapeshifting for free and I'm arguing that this is the source of the problem. If Lunars couldn't get the shape of almost anything under the sun without any investment, then it would be easier to write powers that let them make the most of the shapes they do have. The 2e Knack/Charm paradigm also made it impossible to write charms that were based on shape so that certainly didn't help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T12:11:12-08:00","id":81718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zironic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=81702#post81702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Tell me again how the Water Anima, ERP, JWA, PHB and Scorpion and Toad are die adders, I'd like to hear all about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't actually say such a thing. You said:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zironic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=81702#post81702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it doesn't matter how many thousand dice you can add through charms, you'll never breathe underwater, weave webs, inject deadly venom with your bite or fly like a swallow</div> </div> </div> </div>And I pointed out that you can in fact do all of those things, as a starting character in multiple Exalt types. The fact that all of these are readily done with Lunar Charms, at character creation, is a relatively strong argument that shape-shafting is essentially worthless as-is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T12:20:57-08:00","id":81722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuddenThunder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=81718#post81718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I pointed out that you can in fact do all of those things, as a starting character in multiple Exalt types. The fact that all of these are readily done with Lunar Charms, at character creation, is a relatively strong argument that shape-shafting is essentially worthless as-is.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">It doesn't matter how many thousand dice you can add through charms</span>,</b> you'll never breathe underwater, weave webs, inject deadly venom with your bite or fly like a swallow </div> </div> </div>You used half a dozen charms to emulate subsets of what you can achieve with shapeshifting and you claim this proves that shapeshifting is worthless? What? That's not a strong argument, that's a self-defeating argument.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T12:34:18-08:00","id":81730,"title":"","content":"Anyway can we at least agree that if Lunars need more charms for sneakiness, these charms should absolutely not be in <i>Dexterity</i>?<br /> <br /> As I pointed out, Lunars have tons of sneaky-bastard charms in Manipulation, Appearance, and Charisma. (It's reasonably obvious that eg <i>Clover Can't Be Found</i> is meant to cover a lot of what you want. You might take issue with the design of that charm or argue that it doesn't do enough, but that's another question.)<br /> <br /> But clearly given how Lunar abilities are laid out and given that Dexterity could in theory do basically <i>everything</i>, I think it's clear that the Lunar design chose to instead assign certain capacities to specific abilities as a unique Lunar theme, and that, for Lunars, Dexterity does not generally get sneakiness charms, regardless of its application in Dexterity + Stealth rolls in the larger system. I find it hard to see how anyone could disagree with this decision -- are you going to argue that Dexterity doesn't do enough?<br /> <br /> (Making Lunar sneakiness charms exclusively dependent on social abilities also gives it a unique flavor compared to the Stealth charms of many other splats, which tend to focus on the physical act of sneaking real well. Not everyone should do stealth the same way; there's no reason Lunars should need things like that if eg. Appearance charms like Clover Can't Be Found can cover what's necessary.)<br /> <br /> Notice that these charms tend to focus on situations where you have a reason to want to keep your human form -- they're disguise charms with some stealth applications. I think that makes sense, because, again, if you just want to use straightforward stealth you're probably relying primarily on shapeshifting. (Although Clover Can't Be Found -- conceptually, putting aside arguments over its specific mechanical implementation -- is still very useful either way, whether in human or animal form.)<br /> <br /> Regarding the sneaking-as-a-rat issue -- what do you people think happens if someone rolls successfully to see you as a rat? Seriously. Unless they're looking for a Lunar specifically, their reaction is going to be &quot;ugh, another rat; this job sucks&quot;, not &quot;ugh, a rat; it must be a shapeshifting Anathema!&quot; Assuming you're sneaking into someplace where rats are common (or at least not so rare that a guard will drop everything to hunt one down), it's not a roll that actually matters, because nothing will happen when you fail... so it's not a dramatically-appropriate thing to actually bother rolling.<br /> <br /> Even if they are looking for you, jumping at every single rat is going to cause problems for them. (And you can, with the right knack, become a fly instead. Are they going to treat every fly they spot as a full-scale Anathema invasion?)<br /> <br /> As a ST I might roll to see if they spot you as an innocuous animal, but the only way it would matter is that, the next day when the guards discover what you've done -- and if they realize they were hit by a shapeshifting Anathema -- one of them might slap his forehead and say &quot;That rat! Oh, dammit dammit dammit!&quot; But it will be too late for them to do anything at that point.<br /> <br /> Also notice the particular mechanical intersection of taking an innocuous animal form and using Clover Can't Be Found. If the guards aren't looking for you, they're not going to care about a rat; if they <i>are</i> looking for you, Clover Can't Be Found steps in and makes their job more difficult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 02-28-2014, 03:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T12:45:28-08:00","id":81736,"title":"","content":"The issue with not putting sneaky charms in Dexterity is that you do run into the problem of not being able to favor the attributes needed for your core competency. Though this is fixed by changing how Lunars favor attributes.<br /> <br /> As for the shapeshifting being an auto-success for sneaking, well, yes. And it runs into the exact same problem as putting the &quot;you can't lie to me&quot; charm early on in Integrity, or more apt, the Solar Larceny Tree. Basically, no lunar specializes in Stealth, because they get the auto-win 90% of stealth encounters automatically.<br /> <br /> I mean, I've literally encountered Lunars hiding in a room as a fly on the wall(because screw players). There's not much one can do against that unless you're busting out the really powerful awareness charms, though those have the problem of costing much, much more than a simple shapeshift.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2005-cosar","name":"CoSaR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T12:57:40-08:00","id":81742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zironic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=81722#post81722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not a strong argument, that's a self-defeating argument.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. <br /> <br /> Even the smallest, newest Lunar starts with more than half a dozen Charms. Which means that every Lunar could be better off in every area we've discussed and still have points to spare at start-up. This is not the sign of a healthy alternative power source. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T13:19:25-08:00","id":81749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=81730#post81730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I find it hard to see how anyone could disagree with this decision -- are you going to argue that Dexterity doesn't do enough?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are certainly issues with Dexterity doing too much and being the obvious stat everyone has 5s in. It's not the only one doing too much, in my opinion. That said I do have a issue with teaching people to expect stealth to be governed by Dexterity and then shoving it into Wits. A whimsical and lyrical reinterpretation of the ability spead is one thing (and can probably really only fly once). Playing it all straight but pushing a couple of application into different Traits? Not so cool. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=81730#post81730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the sneaking-as-a-rat issue -- what do you people think happens if someone rolls successfully to see you as a rat?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a great argument, except for the Tell. I'm actually a fan of the Tell and I support it's contention that stealth shouldn't be disguise (If someone spots you despite your creeping, they can recognise it's you) and disguise shouldn't be stealth (dressed as the washerwoman you walk right by the weasls, stopping to chat for a while about the Death-Or-Glory-Toads.). The problem is that neither particularly works on it's own at the moment so the division seems arbitrary and cruel. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T13:31:25-08:00","id":81757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=81525#post81525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In particular, are you still talking about Dexterity when you suggest removing the memory of your presence from somebody's mind?</div> </div> </div> </div>Point of fact, I don't know if he <i>was </i>still talking about Dexterity Charms, or just Lunar Charms in general.<br /> <br /> I do know that Second Edition Lunars had Forgetful Victim Prana for making people forget the next several moments (or few minutes) after they happen. Like a time-delayed Nueralizer that doesn't touch any memories from <i>before </i>the flash. Lunars in both editions also had Mind-Blanking Fear Technique for traumatizing people into forgetting memories completely unrelated to the current situation. Both of these are social Attribute Charms rather than Dexterity.<br /> <br /> I hope that 3rd Edition Lunars have a bit more flexibility and flavor in regards to memory-manipulation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=81479#post81479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More seriously: Lunars do have sneaky charms, but they tend to not be in Dexterity. And, honestly, I think that's a good thing -- you're not seriously suggesting you want Dexterity to do even <i>more</i>, are you? Given the way abilities are structured and the desire to give them a distinctive theme, it makes sense to me that the writers decided that Lunar stealth focused more on (Manipulation, Charisma, etc) trickery and illusion effects rather than Dexterity-style &quot;I sneak real well&quot; charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>At the very least, it makes sense that Dexterity would provide the Lunar way to move silently and to squeeze through cracks or escape out of binds they're not yet small enough to slip through.<br /> <br /> But I said above, yes, social Attribute Charms are better for altering memories of you ever being present at the scene. An Appearance Charm that controls your scent would be good for eliminating one sort of trace of your passage (or laying down a misleading trace). And Lunars can have Wits Charms for the entire concept of &quot;always standing in someone's blindspot&quot; for things like personal stealth and Rats In The Basement army-stealth.<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zironic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=81598#post81598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I think it would be easier to balance if Lunars didn't get &quot;Turn into almost anything!&quot; at chargen, but instead 'Turn into small things like Rats' was a charm in the stealth tree and 'turn into fast things like Cheetahs' was part of the move fast tree etc. It's the front-loaded part that makes it so awkward and also makes it hard for Lunars to distinguish themselves from each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, and I've agreed for a long while. But John and Holden have told us that Lunars don't spend XP to acquire and assume the forms of cheetahs and birds, so they're sticking with that direction with a different idea for making it work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T15:17:09-08:00","id":81783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuddenThunder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=81707#post81707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think of stealthy Lunars and I think of Alien, or Predator, or the Thing. Knowing that you're hunted by something but not knowing what it is, or where it is. Slowly being consumed one by one, not because it can't take you all at once but because it wants to play with you. Maybe it wants to let one of you get away and run back to the Realm with stories of how it terrorised you. Or maybe you'll be the last one left and you'll worship it, because what else can you possibly do?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well there's that. I also feel that there's a proper space for a Lunar turning out to be somewhere where you really don't expect or want them to be...<br /> <br /> But that's really endemic to any kind of stealthiness, isn't it?<br /> <br /> I guess looking at the aforementioned example, I don't quite feel so off about how they're getting in as what they're doing once there.<br /> <br /> ... No, no that's still not right. Becoming something kind of spectral, that still feels like a raksha and Abyssal thing.<br /> <br /> It's hard to grasp at suitable examples at the moment, given prior Editions that have been fairly bad at given textured approaches to stealth in general and distinctive and consistent things for Lunars in particular.<br /> <br /> I suppose, at the most basic level, I can say that I dislike the idea of Lunars having Charms that get too much into them having excessively magical substance. The idea of a Lunar transforming into smoke or light or shadow... it feels somehow incongruent with their core sources. A stealthy Lunar is something I feel should be fast and slick and able to slip into tight places and blend where they shouldn't...<br /> <br /> See, another thing that feels like it's making it hard to distinguish from Solars is that stealth and disguise and all of those kinds of things already inherently go into a space of looking like something you're not. I suppose, from there, I can understand the impulse to want all Solar Stealth to be explicit commands to be ignored, even if I vehemently disagree with it (Solars should be credibly good at all of their skills).<br /> <br /> Though there is some of the obliquely magical stuff as well; misdirection by leaving your skin behind, perhaps. Maybe shaking off a few of your hairs that crawl away as vermin to distract people.<br /> <br /> I don't know... maybe there's a mindspace to be taken from rough draft Infernal Stealth Charms, like turning into a sharp crimson wind, or being invisible and blind and attacking the first thing you bump into.<br /> <br /> Maybe it would also help to approach from an idea that Lunars won't have things that could be explicitly labeled as stealth Charms, even if stealth is their primary function. It's the ultimate purpose, but the motif and the Attribute aren't treating it as the central mechanism...<br /> <br /> Hmm, going back to that idea of more textured stealth challenges, a system or general play/storyteller mindset in which the actual tasks necessary to overcome stealth challenges being more varied would likely be useful. I mean, if it isn't, then the only reason I can ever really see for a Lunar <i>not</i> to just elect to have one or more small animal forms as their way of sneaking around is personal distaste. So I guess that for Charms that help you sneak about to be considered worthwhile compared to that, there needs to be a deeper sense of how you can be spotted or exposed that Charms would be more useful for going against, and a small animal form is there as a fallback for those Lunars not dedicated to facing those challenges.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T17:30:38-08:00","id":81829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuddenThunder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=81749#post81749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a great argument, except for the Tell. I'm actually a fan of the Tell and I support it's contention that stealth shouldn't be disguise (If someone spots you despite your creeping, they can recognise it's you) and disguise shouldn't be stealth (dressed as the washerwoman you walk right by the weasls, stopping to chat for a while about the Death-Or-Glory-Toads.). The problem is that neither particularly works on it's own at the moment so the division seems arbitrary and cruel.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm in the opposite camp. The Tell is a design flaw, what good is shape-shifting when you're easily recognisable? Lunars are all about being seen, their glorious god-bodies. That doesn't mean they're about being recognised. A Lunar's &quot;stealth&quot; is disguise. They are the thing you least expect to be what they are. No one suspects a fly, or a rat, they're vermin under ones notice. Perfect for the Lunar that wants to remain unrecognised.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T17:37:12-08:00","id":81833,"title":"","content":"I believe we were told that Lunar tyrant lizards aren't going to be balancing on tree leaves with a single talon, even when using Graceful Crane Stance or whatever passes for it.<br /> <br /> Assuming that it's true, and Lunars can't use forms in counter-intuitive ways like that, perhaps they NEED to use forms in intuitive ways to get the most of their Charms.<br /> <br /> That is, a &quot;moving silently over gravel, without displacing a pebble&quot; Charm* might be mediocre in human form, impossible as an ox, and only truly effective if using the shape of a cat, mouse or snake.<br /> <br /> Sure, every Lunar can easily have all of those animal forms without spending XP, but the battle-focused Lunar will buy the Charms that work with combat-capable forms, and the infiltrator Lunar will buy the Charms that enhance his use of vermin forms. In this way, the samey Lunars are given a way to distinguish from each other despite their samey-ness.<br /> <br /> <br /> * Incidentally, that seems like a good way to avoid Graceful Crane Stance and Easily Overlooked Presence Method. Give Lunars a &quot;good balance&quot; Charm that provides certain benefits to stealth, without covering ALL the bases of stealth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T17:39:32-08:00","id":81836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=81833#post81833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe we were told that Lunar tyrant lizards aren't going to be balancing on tree leaves with a single talon, even when using Graceful Crane Stance or whatever passes for it.<br /> <br /> Assuming that it's true, and Lunars can't use forms in counter-intuitive ways like that, perhaps they NEED to use forms in intuitive ways to get the most of their Charms.<br /> <br /> That is, a &quot;moving silently over gravel, without displacing a pebble&quot; Charm* might be mediocre in human form, impossible as an ox, and only truly effective if using the shape of a cat, mouse or snake.<br /> <br /> Sure, every Lunar can easily have all of those animal forms without spending XP, but the battle-focused Lunar will buy the Charms that work with combat-capable forms, and the infiltrator Lunar will buy the Charms that enhance his use of vermin forms. In this way, the samey Lunars are given a way to distinguish from each other despite their samey-ness.<br /> <br /> <br /> * Incidentally, that seems like a good way to avoid Graceful Crane Stance and Easily Overlooked Presence Method. Give Lunars a &quot;good balance&quot; Charm that provides certain benefits to stealth, without covering ALL the bases of stealth.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is rather the total opposite direction Lunars are going. Lunars are going to be just as effective not as shapeshifters as they are as shapeshifters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T20:05:16-08:00","id":81892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=81829#post81829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm in the opposite camp. The Tell is a design flaw, what good is shape-shifting when you're easily recognisable? Lunars are all about being seen, their glorious god-bodies. That doesn't mean they're about being recognised. A Lunar's &quot;stealth&quot; is disguise. They are the thing you least expect to be what they are. No one suspects a fly, or a rat, they're vermin under ones notice. Perfect for the Lunar that wants to remain unrecognised.</div> </div> </div> </div>By that token, neither Solars nor Infernals should get stealth.<br /> <br /> I mean, why not just remove it from the Lunar sheet if it's not in-theme? Disguises are larceny.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":296,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","user":"hippokrene","date":". 02-28-2014, 11:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T20:15:11-08:00","id":81900,"title":"","content":"I'd like a Lunar charm where I can track someone by their fear.<br /> <br /> Also, I'd like to be able to go into a crowd of people and insight them to tear one of their own members apart.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T20:55:57-08:00","id":81915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=81892#post81892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By that token, neither Solars nor Infernals should get stealth.<br /> <br /> I mean, why not just remove it from the Lunar sheet if it's not in-theme? Disguises are larceny.</div> </div> </div> </div>What? Not at all. The stealth of a Solar/Infernal is thematically different than a Lunar. A Solar using stealth will not be seen. A Lunar using stealth will be seen, but not recognized.<br /> One of the key themes of new Lunars if their glorious god-bodies and how &quot;physical&quot; they are. Not being seen at all, by anyone, is endemic to this theme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T20:59:53-08:00","id":81917,"title":"","content":"On the Tell, I like the Tell in the sense that Lunars have a cool unique feature that makes them look a bit inhuman. My No Moon has Owl eyes, his adopted daughter the Changing Moon has a fox's tail. I think it'd be a shame to lose that.<br /> But in terms of being a weakness in their shapeshifting, it seems a little pointless. There's also the slightly weird thing where you either notice it and it's really obvious, or you don't notice it at all, regardless of what it is. I think the idea is something like you notice that the bird over there only has one eye, like that dog that was following you earlier, and like your nemesis the one-eyed Lunar... maybe it's the Lunar spying on you! IOr maybe not, you're not sure. But it doesn't really work like that in practice, mechanically.<br /> Also, as one of my players who plays Lunars a lot occasionally gripes, when other Exalt types do shapeshifting, they're actually better at it, because they don't have this weakness. Infernals using Loom-Snarling Deception, for example.<br /> <br /> Maybe they should have an animal feature in true human form (possibly with an option not to), but not the Tell itself, to much up their shapeshifting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T21:00:30-08:00","id":81918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=81833#post81833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe we were told that Lunar tyrant lizards aren't going to be balancing on tree leaves with a single talon, even when using Graceful Crane Stance or whatever passes for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't happen in Ex2, either, since the weight limit for &quot;can't happen&quot; balancing is half a ton, and tyrant lizards weight somewhere between 4 and 6 metric tons fully grown.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Assuming that it's true, and Lunars can't use forms in counter-intuitive ways like that, perhaps they NEED to use forms in intuitive ways to get the most of their Charms.<br /> <br /> That is, a &quot;moving silently over gravel, without displacing a pebble&quot; Charm* might be mediocre in human form, impossible as an ox, and only truly effective if using the shape of a cat, mouse or snake.<br /> <br /> Sure, every Lunar can easily have all of those animal forms without spending XP, but the battle-focused Lunar will buy the Charms that work with combat-capable forms, and the infiltrator Lunar will buy the Charms that enhance his use of vermin forms. In this way, the samey Lunars are given a way to distinguish from each other despite their samey-ness.<br /> <br /> <br /> * Incidentally, that seems like a good way to avoid Graceful Crane Stance and Easily Overlooked Presence Method. Give Lunars a &quot;good balance&quot; Charm that provides certain benefits to stealth, without covering ALL the bases of stealth. </div> </div> </div>I'm still pulling for The Cheshire Cat/Predator method.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T21:14:03-08:00","id":81926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=81757#post81757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the very least, it makes sense that Dexterity would provide the Lunar way to move silently and to squeeze through cracks or escape out of binds they're not yet small enough to slip through.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maaaybe. But it seems to me that giving &quot;escape from ropes&quot; or &quot;squeeze through small holes&quot; as a charm to the splat that can turn into a mouse is a bit unnecessary. If your smallest form still doesn't fit, well, get a smaller form... if there's going to be a Lunar charm similar to Door-Evading Technique that just lets you slip through a crack however small it is, I don't think it particularly <i>has</i> to be in Dexterity, and it can probably work via a more interesting mechanism than just being really good at slipping out of bonds. (Eg. turning briefly into mist or something along those lines.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T00:12:25-08:00","id":81978,"title":"","content":"Part of the problem, I think, is that actual characters are supposed to wield custom Charms. I see the core book Charm trees as outlines, giving you a sense of the general theme and power scale, rather than a selection of the actual powers available to any given Lunar. Attributes are far more flexible than Abilities and I feel that this should be reflected in the Charms.<br /> <br /> For instance, a Full Moon brawler might have a set of Spirit-trapping and -killing Charms building off his basic damage enhancers. He doesn't need a ton of Perception to hurt ghosts, that's silly - but on the flip side, no matter how strong he gets, it won't help him see them, much less track invisible ephemeral beings across the millennia.<br /> <br /> That's the sort of thing I'd like to see. Elder Lunars should not have every stat maxed out for the sake of covering all of their bases - but they should take their main Attributes to the limit and find weird and interesting ways of applying them to all situations.<br /> <br /> And, for the record, True Form, Form Lock and the current version of the Tell are all Anathema to be killed with radioactive hate-fire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Aretii: &quot;As one of the players described it, 'After initiation, it was actually a relief seeing who had eyepatches or bandaged hands - you know what <i>they</i> sacrificed, instead of wondering what bits people cut out of their own souls to gain power.'&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/578-lord-sia","name":"Lord Sia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T00:21:37-08:00","id":81983,"title":"","content":"Today, I decided I wanted to make a Lunar with a jaguar spirit shape. She would be a sleek and deadly jungle predator, gliding effortlessly through the trees as she tracked down her pray, striking with elegant precision, and then melting back into the shadows.<br /> <br /> Does the Attribute bump for DBT count for Charm minimums if as long as I only use the charm while in that form? I went 3/5/3 for physical attributes, and there's a surprising number of charms that are only strength 4 or 5.<br /> <br /> Blood on the Wind and Inevitable Spoor Discovery seem suited to being a master predator.<br /> <br /> I'm starting to understand that with Lunars, you work backwards. Usually, I come up with a character concept, slap down relevant abilities and attributes, and then pick charms. Lunars work better when you start with the charms and build your character around them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T02:22:50-08:00","id":82020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=81900#post81900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like a Lunar charm where I can track someone by their fear.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the idea of Lunars approaching something a bit abstract or esoteric through the logos of their animalistic or fearsome qualities feels rather suitable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=81900#post81900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I'd like to be able to go into a crowd of people and insight them to tear one of their own members apart.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thinking of stuff like this, and how Sunder referenced those Charms where the target isn't going to remember the next few minutes, I feel like I can ease some of my problems with Lunar direct emotion control by imagining Charms where the Lunar is or does a thing that provokes a specific, Essence-defined response from people. Like an Intelligence or Wits Charm to stir yourself into a manic frenzy in attacking somebody that everybody who sees you is so dreadfully compelled by that they join in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=81926#post81926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it seems to me that giving &quot;escape from ropes&quot; or &quot;squeeze through small holes&quot; as a charm to the splat that can turn into a mouse is a bit unnecessary. If your smallest form still doesn't fit, well, get a smaller form...</div> </div> </div> </div>This is where I feel like a distinction between a Lunar dedicated to escape and evasion and one who isn't might help.<br /> <br /> I mean, fundamentally, somebody who tries to confine you in a manner that you can escape by turning into a mouse or something is somebody who probably didn't know that you were a Lunar, because somebody who did know that will probably try trapping you in something that you can't just escape by becoming a small animal (or, if you do, they'll make you pay for it), which might then require more magical methods to get out of.<br /> <br /> Any Lunar can have the capacity to turn into a tyrant lizard, but tyrant lizards can't really fight in all places, so it's not exactly an all-purpose solution.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=81926#post81926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it particularly <i>has</i> to be in Dexterity, and it can probably work via a more interesting mechanism than just being really good at slipping out of bonds. (Eg. turning briefly into mist or something along those lines.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like the premise that already assumes that means that present the physicality of the Lunars is a premise that won't really match well with Lunars who use glorious god-bodies rather than illusions.<br /> <br /> Not that turning into something kind of insubstantial necessarily strays too far (it at least reminds me of the Captain from Hellsing), but still worth keeping in mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T02:51:14-08:00","id":82024,"title":"","content":"There are some charms where Lunar's travel through 'tunnels in the Wyld' to get around.<br /> <br /> I wonder if there's a way that a Lunar can create multiple territories and travel from one to another. I'm not talking Creation-wide, but something faster than turning into a bird and flying there. Traveling through 'shadows' at night or entering a trance and traveling through 'dreams.'<br /> <br /> Can someone give me a reference for the glorious god-body we're all chatting about? While DBT is awesome and Lunar spirit shape is interesting, I am unsure where this specific idea is coming from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T03:36:06-08:00","id":82028,"title":"","content":"Well, there's Walking on Moonlight (Wits 5, Essence 4), which lets you, well, walk on moonlight from one piece of your territory to another territory you own.<br /> <br /> As to Glorious God-Body, I think that's from Scroll of Heroes, it's a merit for God-Blood that works, IIRC, like the 1st ed DBT, ie you get 3 dots to split between your physical attributes, rather than +1 to each of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T03:39:44-08:00","id":82029,"title":"","content":"My thanks, Wiz.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T04:05:54-08:00","id":82034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=82020#post82020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like the premise that already assumes that means that present the physicality of the Lunars is a premise that won't really match well with Lunars who use glorious god-bodies rather than illusions.<br /> <br /> Not that turning into something kind of insubstantial necessarily strays too far (it at least reminds me of the Captain from Hellsing), but still worth keeping in mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not think that the Lunar charmset should provide any more support than is absolutely necessary for Lunars whose desire is simply &quot;I want to use my glorious human physical stats in human form in the most straightforward way imaginable.&quot; The problem is that that thematic (&quot;straightforward application of [attribute]&quot;) is, the vast majority of the time, going to be completely indistinguishable from &quot;straightforward application of [ability]&quot; for any ability / attribute pairing, and we already have massive numbers of people mining that extremely narrow and relatively boring territory. Obviously Lunars can't avoid touching on it occasionally, but if there is any way at all that something can be covered by another Lunar thematic, they should get that approach instead -- the Lunar thematic should be <i>heavily</i> about master cunning shapeshifter, trickster lord of illusions; and very little about Strongdude the Super-Strong Dude. The fact is that we got the charmset of Strongdude the Super-Strong Dude as a big part of the (usable) Lunar charmset in the past two editions, and it was mostly a boring regurgitation of charms that had already been published elsewhere with the power level mildly tweaked.<br /> <br /> Obviously that doesn't mean I don't think they should get charms that play up their physical attributes at times, but given the choice between a Lunar charm for escaping bonds by being extra-nimble, or having them do something with a more obvious shapeshifting-trickster theme, I would always prefer to go for the latter.<br /> <br /> But also, thinking about it, I take issue with your assertion that a Lunar shouldn't rely on shapeshifting to escape bonds because someone who knows they're a shapeshifter will use special anti-shapeshifting measures. If you're talking about specific magical bonds that defeat shapeshifting automatically, those constraints shouldn't exist. If they do -- well, what on earth is their purpose? They're special shackles that explicitly only exist to bind Lunars; clearly it makes no sense to allow those special anti-Lunar shackles and then give Lunars a way to defeat them. Trying to imprison a Lunar is probably going to involve more esoteric things like sealing them in a room with no entrances or exits, or dropping a mountain on them that always weighs a bit more than they can lift, or casting them into an infinite abyss or the like. And if you're talking about that, there shouldn't be any one charm that will solve the situation -- obviously using an &quot;I escape anyway!&quot; charm is not going to be satisfactory. In general, weird hyper-specific prisons like that seem like they're still probably best approached with shapeshifting, since the best way to get out is by having a power your jailor didn't anticipate, and shapeshifting is far better at that than charms simply because you can have many more shapes than charms.<br /> <br /> More generally, it seems to me that imprisoning a Lunar in a prison that is completely impervious to shapeshifting seems to me like it would be at least as hard as imprisoning any other type of Exalt in a prison that completely thwarts their charms.<br /> <br /> (Lunars are in general among the hardest Exalted to imprison because of this, of course.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T04:14:14-08:00","id":82036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=82024#post82024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can someone give me a reference for the glorious god-body we're all chatting about? While DBT is awesome and Lunar spirit shape is interesting, I am unsure where this specific idea is coming from.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was a thing M\u00f8rke said. Basically, Lunars are supposed to have very physical Charms, deriving from shapeshifting, raw might and charisma, and &quot;bodily&quot; passions rather than esoteric concepts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T04:24:09-08:00","id":82040,"title":"","content":"Oh, that's what people were talking about? Oops. Sorry Hippokrene, this is what happens when you come back to a forum after two years and have no idea what people are talking about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=82034#post82034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not think that the Lunar charmset should provide any more support than is absolutely necessary for Lunars whose desire is simply &quot;I want to use my glorious human physical stats in human form in the most straightforward way imaginable.&quot; The problem is that that thematic (&quot;straightforward application of [attribute]&quot;) is, the vast majority of the time, going to be completely indistinguishable from &quot;straightforward application of [ability]&quot; for any ability / attribute pairing, and we already have massive numbers of people mining that extremely narrow and relatively boring territory. Obviously Lunars can't avoid touching on it occasionally, but if there is any way at all that something can be covered by another Lunar thematic, they should get that approach instead -- the Lunar thematic should be <i>heavily</i> about master cunning shapeshifter, trickster lord of illusions; and very little about Strongdude the Super-Strong Dude. The fact is that we got the charmset of Strongdude the Super-Strong Dude as a big part of the (usable) Lunar charmset in the past two editions, and it was mostly a boring regurgitation of charms that had already been published elsewhere with the power level mildly tweaked.</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely agree with you. My favourite charms in 2nd ed were the esoteric ones, the ones where you changed your body, not just did things a Solar could do. For example, of the 3 physical attributes, stamina was my favourite, with stuff like swallowing poisons and learning how to produce them, or growing bone plates out of your skin to protect you. Whereas Dexterity was mostly just repackaged Solar charms with higher prereqs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T05:17:19-08:00","id":82056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=82036#post82036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was a thing M\u00f8rke said. Basically, Lunars are supposed to have very physical Charms, deriving from shapeshifting, raw might and charisma, and &quot;bodily&quot; passions rather than esoteric concepts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=82034#post82034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not think that the Lunar charmset should provide any more support than is absolutely necessary for Lunars whose desire is simply &quot;I want to use my glorious human physical stats in human form in the most straightforward way imaginable.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the Lunar charmset should be built around Lunar themes and sometimes those themes are straightforward.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=82034#post82034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...the Lunar thematic should be <i>heavily</i> about master cunning shapeshifter, trickster lord of illusions; and very little about Strongdude the Super-Strong Dude. The fact is that we got the charmset of Strongdude the Super-Strong Dude as a big part of the (usable) Lunar charmset in the past two editions, and it was mostly a boring regurgitation of charms that had already been published elsewhere with the power level mildly tweaked.</div> </div> </div> </div>The ravenous beastman who falls upon you, tears you limb-from-limb, and devours your entrails is as valid a Lunar concept as the master cunning trickster, lord of illusions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=82034#post82034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obviously that doesn't mean I don't think they should get charms that play up their physical attributes at times, but given the choice between a Lunar charm for escaping bonds by being extra-nimble, or having them do something with a more obvious shapeshifting-trickster theme, I would always prefer to go for the latter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunars are more than shapeshifter-tricksters though. It feels as though that's the only aspect of them that you appreciate.<br /> <br /> Here are some ways that Lunars could escape a bond:<br /> 1. Shapeshift into a mouse<br /> 2. Chew through their wrists and ankles and immediately regrow the lost limbs.<br /> 3. Summon a swarm of vermin to chew through their bond or to bring the Lunar a key.<br /> 4. Mimic the voice of a guard, causing another guard to momentarily believe that the Lunar has escaped, and that she should free her buddy.<br /> 5. Sing to the little god of the lock, causing it to open on its own.<br /> 6. Identify a weak chain, and then regurgitate the purified venom of the brass-eating roach to burn through the metal.<br /> 7. Blend into the cell so well that the guards no longer see him and when they come to investigate, pounce.<br /> <br /> For me, 1 is the most boring. But what I've gotten from you is that options 2-7 shouldn't be charms because a Lunar can shapeshift into a mouse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":296,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","user":"hippokrene","date":". 03-01-2014, 08:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T05:44:25-08:00","id":82064,"title":"","content":"Lunars are not about illusions. They're all about physicality, about their body doing things, their body changing and blending. Not summoning false images to trick the mind. There is no trickery, the Lunar is physically what it appears to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T06:43:21-08:00","id":82079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=82034#post82034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not think that the Lunar charmset should provide any more support than is absolutely necessary for Lunars whose desire is simply &quot;I want to use my glorious human physical stats in human form in the most straightforward way imaginable.&quot; The problem is that that thematic (&quot;straightforward application of [attribute]&quot;) is, the vast majority of the time, going to be completely indistinguishable from &quot;straightforward application of [ability]&quot; for any ability / attribute pairing, and we already have massive numbers of people mining that extremely narrow and relatively boring territory. Obviously Lunars can't avoid touching on it occasionally, but if there is any way at all that something can be covered by another Lunar thematic, they should get that approach instead -- the Lunar thematic should be <i>heavily</i> about master cunning shapeshifter, trickster lord of illusions; and very little about Strongdude the Super-Strong Dude. The fact is that we got the charmset of Strongdude the Super-Strong Dude as a big part of the (usable) Lunar charmset in the past two editions, and it was mostly a boring regurgitation of charms that had already been published elsewhere with the power level mildly tweaked.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there's some swing room between &quot;basically just doing Solar stuff&quot; and &quot;turning into mist&quot;.<br /> <br /> That said, Lunars will likely have Strength Charms; it feels slightly counter-intuitive for that not to at least occasionally amount to them hitting something really hard with their fists (even if it's conveyed in a visual motif of their fist being coated in moonsilver or something).<br /> <br /> Though mostly, I just want them to live up to this promise:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I want a Lunar swordsman who is just as capable in a fight as a Lunar going full-time DBT. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obviously that doesn't mean I don't think they should get charms that play up their physical attributes at times, but given the choice between a Lunar charm for escaping bonds by being extra-nimble, or having them do something with a more obvious shapeshifting-trickster theme, I would always prefer to go for the latter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would prefer for there not to be a perception of dichotomy between them. If the Lunar twists their way out in a manner that is obliquely reshaping their body, without getting too far out of shapeshifter hero/primal god theme space.<br /> <br /> I mean, I think that's always been my problem with idea like wanting Lunars to turn into a ball of light or an emotion or something to me; those things don't feel like shapeshifter stuff to me, even if they technically involve your physical shape changing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But also, thinking about it, I take issue with your assertion that a Lunar shouldn't rely on shapeshifting to escape bonds because someone who knows they're a shapeshifter will use special anti-shapeshifting measures. If you're talking about specific magical bonds that defeat shapeshifting automatically, those constraints shouldn't exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the outset, I'm thinking about bonds that work on the same principle as clothes (or rather, armour) that allow Lunars to shapeshift without having to become naked.<br /> <br /> That is to say, yeah you've shapeshifted... into a mouse who is also tied up in chains. Fucking moonsilver.<br /> <br /> There's other stuff too, like surrounding them with mousetraps. Something that might take advantage of the vulnerability of a small shape the way hiding in a building can take advantage of the shortcomings of a tyrant lizard.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, something like that contraption Tai Lung was shackled in; that fucker looks like it would fall on top of you if you turned into a mouse, and suddenly you're under a giant shell of stone and jade (also you get pulled taut by the weights hanging over the precipice).<br /> <br /> (Incidentally, substitute legs for a tail, and then have him grabbing at stray feathers and using them to jimmy the lock open by impossibly contorting your foot up to it, that feels like a way to get loose and reference transformation motifs without turning into an animal or something out of theme)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they do -- well, what on earth is their purpose? They're special shackles that explicitly only exist to bind Lunars</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Lunars aren't the only things capable of shapeshifting.<br /> <br /> But more importantly:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">clearly it makes no sense to allow those special anti-Lunar shackles and then give Lunars a way to defeat them.</div> </div> </div> </div>It references how a Lunar who can shapeshift into a small animals is a lot more likely than a Lunar who has Charms to deal with this situation.<br /> <br /> I mean, I like shapeshifting, but when it's used as an excuse to cordon off thing for Lunars to have Charms to do, I understand the hostility towards it, especially since, barring a significant future revision towards it, we know that shapeshifting is giving Lunars advantages that they generally don't have to pay XP for.<br /> <br /> That and, well, Charms are part of the whole fun of Exalts; the big shopping lists of exception-based powers. Things that are sneaking or evading or even fighting feel like they should be part of that, and for them not to be just because the Lunar can shapeshift... barring a highly interesting execution, it just doesn't sit right with me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In general, weird hyper-specific prisons like that seem like they're still probably best approached with shapeshifting, since the best way to get out is by having a power your jailor didn't anticipate, and shapeshifting is far better at that than charms simply because you can have many more shapes than charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>This here, this is my problem; I like shapeshifting, and I like Charms, and I do not like shapeshifting being used to undermine Charms, because Charms are part of the fun, and it makes shapeshifting look bad.<br /> <br /> Don't really care for the setup where an effective prison for a Lunar or any other Exalt has to be one that covers all of their powers, such that their escape is predicated on a secret power, neither. It's way too binary, the paranoia combat of prison design. No, wait, worse, it's the Flaws of Invulnerability of it.<br /> <br /> There's too much that's interesting in setting up a prison, or any other scenario, where you overcome it with effective and judicious use of the powers you have, rather than cycling through them uselessly until you stumble upon the one that arbitrarily breaks through.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T06:51:41-08:00","id":82083,"title":"","content":"None of Hippokrene's options are about illusions.<br /> <br /> A strong jaw and regeneration are aspects of physicallity. as are mimmicry (altering one's throat and mouth to match someone else's voice), camouflage (blending into teh cell), finding weakness, regurgitating acid.<br /> <br /> Summoning verins and appeasing little gods are not necesarrilly physical but you can't (or at least don't need to )exclude thse form the lunar's repertuare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2245-quimeradc","name":"Quimeradc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T07:39:06-08:00","id":82102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=81900#post81900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like a Lunar charm where I can track someone by their fear.</div> </div> </div> </div>An interesting notion. How is this different from tracking by scent? Do you detect a spiritual trace of fear even in the absence of a physical scent trail? Is it a trail that you smell as opposed to a &quot;beacon&quot; that you &quot;feel&quot; pointing you in the right direction? Do they leave this trail behind as long as they harbor an Intimacy of Fear for you, or as long as they feel fear in general, or both?<br /> <br /> Does it need to be limited to fear, or can you track people by the trail of their love for you?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, I'd like to be able to go into a crowd of people and insight them to tear one of their own members apart. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Incite&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=81915#post81915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the key themes of new Lunars if their glorious god-bodies and how &quot;physical&quot; they are. Not being seen at all, by anyone, is endemic to this theme.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that this prevents a Lunar from investing five dots and some specialties into the Stealth Ability, or using it together with the forms of small and/or nimble creatures to avoid detection. But yeah, since Lunars do not derive Charms from Abilities, they cannot have Stealth Charms as such, and their disguise Charms are not Larceny Charms.<br /> <br /> But even so, I find it hard to believe that moving silently, leaving no prints and avoiding line-of-sight are things that Attribute Charms cannot improve, even obliquely. I'm not expecting Lunars to pass invisibly right in front of someone's face, but superhuman grace, speed and awareness have to have <i>some </i>application to evading notice.<br /> <br /> At least the &quot;leave no scent-trail&quot; stealth trick is easily accomplished as a disguise trick with a scent-alteration Charm.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 03-01-2014, 10:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T21:41:51-08:00","id":82962,"title":"","content":"I can understand people wanting Lunars to be physical; wild, ravenous beasts that tear through everything in their path and devour their prey. I can also understand people wanting Lunars to be trickster illusionists, master shapeshifters who mess with memories and emotions and perceptions to get what they want or just for their own amusement.<br /> <br /> What I don't get is people demanding that Lunars be one or the other. It's almost as if people have forgotten that Luna is whatever the feck she wants to be - and so too are her Chosen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Aretii: &quot;As one of the players described it, 'After initiation, it was actually a relief seeing who had eyepatches or bandaged hands - you know what <i>they</i> sacrificed, instead of wondering what bits people cut out of their own souls to gain power.'&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/578-lord-sia","name":"Lord Sia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T23:35:41-08:00","id":83008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Sia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=82962#post82962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can understand people wanting Lunars to be physical; wild, ravenous beasts that tear through everything in their path and devour their prey. I can also understand people wanting Lunars to be trickster illusionists, master shapeshifters who mess with memories and emotions and perceptions to get what they want or just for their own amusement.<br /> <br /> What I don't get is people demanding that Lunars be one or the other. It's almost as if people have forgotten that Luna is whatever the feck she wants to be - and so too are her Chosen.</div> </div> </div> </div>We need to divide actual physical-ness from violence. I mean physical in that it's very raw, and very real. Lunars have an animalistic feeling, a primal or barbaric theme to them. This does not preclude them from sophistiction or high society at all. It makes them pragmatic or very visceral. They can still be tricksters by actually changing their body, not an illusion that is required to be believed. I maintain Lunar shapeshifting powers should have no UMI effects or tests to overcome, because the Lunar is literally what you see before you. There is no illusion being forced into your mind, or magical disguise, the Lunar is very much what she appears to be.<br /> <br /> With Solars its divine power, this magical thing that they manipulate for effect. It's an energy within them they use to improve their skills and do great feats, but they don't physically change. A Lunar does, a Lunar combines their divine power into physical form. It isn't an energy or magic, it's all within their body, their potential and power is as physical as they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T00:14:50-08:00","id":83021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=83008#post83008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I maintain Lunar shapeshifting powers should have no UMI effects or tests to overcome, because the Lunar is literally what you see before you.</div> </div> </div> </div>UMI as it was often perceived/presented, absolutely. In principle, not so much. I mean, taking a look at Luna's write-up, the ability <i>Beauty to Break All Hearts:</i><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Glories of the Most High: Luna, p. 10</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whenever Luna makes a social attack to build an Intimacy toward herself in another, the influence is unnatural and success forms the attachment instantly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the intended reading there is more that &quot;Luna's presence has such grace and natural charm that only those with great willpower can resist feeling about her however she wishes,&quot; and less that, &quot;Luna's presence sends magic mind control lasers to make those without great willpower feel about her however she wishes.&quot; Lunar Charms that mechanically represent a Lunar achieving the former, in being just so compelling/beautiful/awesome that <i>not</i> feeling for the Lunar demands Willpower expenditure, are perfectly fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T05:31:36-08:00","id":83102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=81673#post81673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People tell stories about freaking everything.<br /> Which stories? What things in particular?That's pretty vague.</div> </div> </div> </div> The urban legend/myth idea wasn't meant to be a complete framework it was meant to be an element that informed how they should be written to keep them from being knockoffs of another Exalt type. Yeah, its a bit vague in the same way that saying Solars should be direct and in your face is vague. Maybe I shouldn't have removed the Solar comparison after all...<br /> <br /> I guess what I am trying to say is that limiting Lunars in such a way that the method of their powers is always Physical, or always Shapeshifting, or always anything is a bad idea because it removes the mystery. It is showing the monster. I'm not saying Lunars need to do things in the exact same way as their patron, but Luna is perhaps the most strange and otherworldly of the Incarna and I'd really like to see that reflected in her children.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T05:35:16-08:00","id":83106,"title":"","content":"Luna is actually really, really straightforward. The Maidens are strange. Luna's main trick is that she can turn into an abominable god-monster with horrendously inflated stats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2418-the-perfect","name":"The Perfect","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T06:05:41-08:00","id":83127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=83102#post83102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess what I am trying to say is that limiting Lunars in such a way that the method of their powers is always Physical, or always Shapeshifting, or always anything is a bad idea because it removes the mystery. It is showing the monster. I'm not saying Lunars need to do things in the exact same way as their patron, but Luna is perhaps the most strange and otherworldly of the Incarna and I'd really like to see that reflected in her children.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Unconquered Sun is being made a more distant and mysterious figure, but nobody is inclined towards the idea that this should mean that Solar Charms oriented to him shouldn't be there.<br /> <br /> Luna and Lunars should not be so otherworldly that you don't know how to actually play them. Physicality does not preclude otherworldliness or mystery anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T06:11:11-08:00","id":83132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=83127#post83127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Unconquered Sun is being made a more distant and mysterious figure, but nobody is inclined towards the idea that this should mean that Solar Charms oriented to him shouldn't be there.<br /> Luna and Lunars should not be so otherworldly that you don't know how to actually play them. Physicality does not preclude otherworldliness or mystery anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div> You thought I wanted another broken unworkable charm set? Hell no. I want one that evokes the mysterious and the otherworldly (among other things) not one that is itself mysterious and otherworldly.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T07:33:38-08:00","id":83155,"title":"","content":"Fair enough. I myself push that in terms of the Lunars having psychedelic qualities; the esoterica that takes place within, rather than being imposed without. I think this fits nicely with the stated themes of rage and transformation, and it internally resonates with the motifs of physicality and the shapeshifter.<br /> <br /> There's a place for the Lunar who fights by changing the form of hir body, but I also think there can be the Lunar who fights as though possessed by a thousand devils without just being Silver Solar.<br /> <br /> Hmm, I think that might actually provide the missing link in that problem of the Lunar Dexterity escape Charms. A Lunar who slips their bonds because they're just good enough? A bit sparse. But a Lunar who slips their bonds by twisting and contorting like they're a character from an exorcism movie?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 03-03-2014, 10:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T07:56:43-08:00","id":83167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=83155#post83155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair enough. I myself push that in terms of the Lunars having psychedelic qualities; the esoterica that takes place within, rather than being imposed without. I think this fits nicely with the stated themes of rage and transformation, and it internally resonates with the motifs of physicality and the shapeshifter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of like them being to manipulate the world around them to a point, (metal fears me and will refuse to hold me) but I wouldn't be too upset if they just changed their relationship with the world (bonds provide no barrier to one such as I)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=83155#post83155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But a Lunar who slips their bonds by twisting and contorting like they're a character from an exorcism movie?</div> </div> </div> </div>That one hits a really good tone, I like it.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T09:47:44-08:00","id":83256,"title":"","content":"The story of a Lunar Exalt is the story of a man, who becomes a monster. At first, that monster is in the form of a beast, but then he progresses into truly monstrous forms like the chimera or hydra. But unlike those simple creatures, the Lunar can flee from Herakles by turning into a bird when the fight turns bad.<br /> <br /> Hmm. If Herakles had a truly Lunar opponent then, perhaps all of the monsters he fought as part of his Labors were really the same Lunar? Rather than killing each one, Herakles only forced the Lunar to retreat to survive and fight another day. Each time, the Lunar tried a new form.<br /> <br /> The Lunar might also have been the queen of the Amazons that I think Herakles had to serve for one Labor.<br /> <br /> <br /> But as part of this story of the man who becomes a monster, how does a monster-man progress?<br /> <br /> As the quintessential human heroes, Morke designed the Solars to gain the most competence at the start of a path (Essence 1), with slow progress (Essence 2, Essence 4) that is interspersed with massive spikes of epiphany (Essence 3, Essence 5).<br /> <br /> But how does a monster-man grow?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 03-03-2014, 12:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T10:25:40-08:00","id":83291,"title":"","content":"One of the things I remember hearing people speculate a while ago that I really liked was the idea of Lunars having multiple personae like the Black Beast of the Eastern Marshes or the Wanderer of Forgotten Paths that most people would think were completely separate entities. I believe the idea was an outgrowth of another one about each of the True Forms being a legend in their own right. Whatever the case, the idea that each of the labors was the same Lunar reminded me of that and I like the idea a lot.<br /> <br /> As for progression, we don't define monsters as much by their own capabilities as much as their danger to us. I think each significant step a Lunar takes (whatever Essence levels are chosen) should amplify and broaden how dangerous a Lunar can be and remove potential impediments that could stand in its way. I'd space that growth a little more evenly to provide more moments where the beast just got a whole lot more dangerous.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T12:03:32-08:00","id":83349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=83256#post83256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The story of a Lunar Exalt is the story of a man, who becomes a monster. At first, that monster is in the form of a beast, but then he progresses into truly monstrous forms like the chimera or hydra. But unlike those simple creatures, the Lunar can flee from Herakles by turning into a bird when the fight turns bad.<br /> <br /> Hmm. If Herakles had a truly Lunar opponent then, perhaps all of the monsters he fought as part of his Labors were really the same Lunar? Rather than killing each one, Herakles only forced the Lunar to retreat to survive and fight another day. Each time, the Lunar tried a new form.<br /> <br /> The Lunar might also have been the queen of the Amazons that I think Herakles had to serve for one Labor.</div> </div> </div> </div>He was actually tasked with capturing Hippolyta's girdle, and Hippolyta does not survive the story.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But as part of this story of the man who becomes a monster, how does a monster-man progress?<br /> <br /> As the quintessential human heroes, Morke designed the Solars to gain the most competence at the start of a path (Essence 1), with slow progress (Essence 2, Essence 4) that is interspersed with massive spikes of epiphany (Essence 3, Essence 5).<br /> <br /> But how does a monster-man grow? </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IRhbOFlTA5g\" target=\"_blank\">Being loved?</a><br /> <br /> While 1e DBT was 1e DBT, it did put forward a statement of Lunars having a huge advantage and experiencing constant growth beyond it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T21:34:22-08:00","id":83757,"title":"","content":"I thought about this thread today.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=81833#post81833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe we were told that Lunar tyrant lizards aren't going to be balancing on tree leaves with a single talon, even when using Graceful Crane Stance or whatever passes for it.<br /> <br /> Assuming that it's true, and Lunars can't use forms in counter-intuitive ways like that, perhaps they NEED to use forms in intuitive ways to get the most of their Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>When in doubt, shapeshift into a Tyrant Lizard.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">When not in doubt... shapeshift into a Tyrant Lizard.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://31.media.tumblr.com/ed8712b939011b7c249ca94b214cbca1/tumblr_inline_n1wcm2xUcQ1r3l3z8.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T10:39:29-08:00","id":84052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=83349#post83349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He was actually tasked with capturing Hippolyta's girdle, and Hippolyta does not survive the story.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neither do most of the other major figures of Herakles' Labors.<br /> <br /> Pretty much the only things he doesn't kill are the ones he explicitly had to bring back alive.<br /> <br /> My premise was that, if Solar Herakles didn't actually kill any of the monsters because they were the same Lunar who always escaped when the fight turned bad, then that Lunar could also be Queen Hippolyta.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-15T11:50:33-07:00","id":91766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=81371#post81371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Today I thought to myself, &quot;I am going to make a sneaky rat lunar.'<br /> <br /> ...it means putting points in dexterity, stealth, and larceny, and then realizing there are no dexterity charms that help with sneaking someplace, breaking into places, or opening locks. The best I could find was an appearance charm that might help me escape detection after people are already alert to my PC's presence and looking for her, and some wits charms that might help me pickpocket things.</div> </div> </div> </div>You forget Perception Charms.<br /> <br /> Keen Sense Technique, Eye of the Cat and All-Encompassing Sorcerer's Sight are dead useful for detecting traps and guardians and other surprises, as well as for finding the thing you mean to steal.<br /> <br /> Eye and Fingertip Wisdom, at Essence 3, allows you to glean an entire structure's floor plan, including chambers that would otherwise be hidden, merely by touching any part of the building. At Essence 2, it at least allows you to know exactly what is in a box before breaking it open.<br /> <br /> Sense-Borrowing Method. Use this on unsuspecting visitors or guards, or on vermin and pests you send in as spies.<br /> <br /> Leaf-Falling Scrutiny. Determine how many dots in Awareness a particular guard has, or how many guards around you have Awareness ratings at least as high as 3, all before you even begin to pit your Stealth rolls against their dice. This Charm can also be useful when screening your <i>Ocean's 11</i> band of thieves to determine which applicants have the skills sufficient for their roles.<br /> <br /> Flaw-Finding Examination, for Lunars without Strength Charms who are also not in a position to use large animal forms. With this Charm, a Lunar in the shape of a rat can chew through steel barriers. Or provide the last necessary advantage for breaking into something that even a large form and Strength Charms just aren't powerful enough to crack on their own.<br /> <br /> Monkey Shaping Emulation, for leaving behind counterfeits so that your victims don't even realize you stole from them... among other uses a thief can find for counterfeits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-15T17:58:18-07:00","id":91994,"title":"","content":"Was The Spider's Trap Door ever meant to set up general sneaking? It seems like it might be able to, but it's so vague that it could go either way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-16T07:30:05-07:00","id":92277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=91994#post91994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was The Spider's Trap Door ever meant to set up general sneaking? It seems like it might be able to, but it's so vague that it could go either way.</div> </div> </div> </div> After exploring how that Charm would actually work and all of its possible applications, I split it into at least two Charms. It was that strong, and needed that many clarifications as limits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-20T23:20:18-07:00","id":95427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/78496-a-couple-simple-thoughts-on-lunars?p=81371#post81371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A simple thought on Lunars:<br /> <br /> Today I thought to myself, &quot;I am going to make a sneaky rat lunar.'<br /> <br /> For a Solar exalted, this would mean I'd need to put points in dexterity, stealth, and larceny, and buy stealth and larceny charms.<br /> <br /> For a Lunar, it means putting points in dexterity, stealth, and larceny, and then realizing there are no dexterity charms that help with sneaking someplace, breaking into places, or opening locks. The best I could find was an appearance charm that might help me escape detection after people are already alert to my PC's presence and looking for her, and some wits charms that might help me pickpocket things.<br /> <br /> I find it odd there are no charms that help you blend into your environment or muffle the noises as they're both very animalish.<br /> <br /> Anyways, I ended up pulling out my copy of Werewolf: The Forsaken, and making a starting Irraka instead.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Hybrid Body Rearrangement.</b> If you weren't aware of it before, it'll probably be your favorite Knack from now on. Use to manifest an unlimited number of mutations that last indefinitely. Some useful options while sneaking:<ul><li><i>Chameleon:</i> Active camouflage, bonus to stealth (2e core).</li> <li><i>Night vision:</i> See in the dark, okay but you can do better (COCD: Wyld).</li> <li><i>Sonar:</i> The Night Caste thinks he's invisible. Stunt yourself a Predator heartbeat while using this (COTD: West).</li> <li><i>Shark sight:</i> Identify visible and invisible creatures in a 360 degree radius out to a considerable range. Prevents a lot of unpleasantness. (COTD: West).</li> </ul><br /> ...And various others. Also use it to enhance natural weapons and armor, grow wings or limbs, walk on ceilings, breathe underwater, gain acid blood or just look freakishly bizarre. There's really no upper limit to the potential usefulness of HBR.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Note the improved errata version.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 03-21-2014, 03:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}